# Cursor Instructions for Website V3

## Architecture Overview

A multi-site, content-driven marketing platform: Vite + React (client, SSR), Express (server), YAML content per site. Page content lives in YAML under each site's content folder, not in the app database.

### Key Structure
- **Client** (`client/src/`): React pages, section components, hooks, contexts
- **Server** (`server/`): Express routes, entry loading/delivery, SSR, GitHub content sync, MCP support
- **Shared** (`shared/`): Zod schemas, shared component registry, locale and slug helpers
- **Sites** ([sites.yml](sites.yml)): each site has a `content_folder` (`site_4geeks-com`, `site_4geeks-florida`, `site_business-4geeks`), gitignored in the app repo and synced to that site's content GitHub repo (`github_repo_url`)

### Sites and inheritance
- `inherit_components_from: <parent folder>` — the child site uses the parent's site component registry and, when the child has no `theme.json` of its own, the parent's theme (whole file, no merge).
- `fallback_content_folder: <parent folder>` — images fall back to the parent folder.

### Content Organization
Entries follow `site_<name>/{contentType}/{slug}/`:
- `_common.yml` — locale-independent metadata
- `en.yml`, `es.yml` — locale files (`normalizeLocale()` in [shared/locale.ts](shared/locale.ts))
- `<variant>.<locale>.yml` — A/B variants; `draft.<locale>.yml` — drafts; `versioning.yml` — version history
- Content types and URL patterns: `site_<name>/content-types.yml` (read via [server/content-types.ts](server/content-types.ts)). Some types are database-backed (cached items plus YAML overrides under `site_<name>/db/`).

## Critical Developer Workflows

### Build & Run
```bash
npm run dev          # Dev server (Vite + Express SSR); predev runs ensure:registry / ensure:schema-yml
npm run build        # Client (Vite) + server (esbuild to dist/)
npm start            # Production build (dist/index.js)
npm run check        # TypeScript check
npm test             # vitest (also the pre-push hook)
```

The server is bundled separately with esbuild (ESM). Development uses `tsx`.

### Editing content
- Staff edit in the in-page editor; edits go through `/api/content/edit-sections` and `/api/content/edit-common` ([server/routes/sections.ts](server/routes/sections.ts)), then Cloud Sync commits to the content repo.
- Agents edit through MCP tools, or edit `site_*` files and push them to the content repo with a SHA ([site-content-github.mdc](.cursor/rules/site-content-github.mdc)).

## Loading Content (server)

- [server/entry-layer.ts](server/entry-layer.ts) — `loadEntry`: one merge for static and database-backed entries (template layers → entry layer → variables). Read-only.
- [server/entry-delivery.ts](server/entry-delivery.ts) — `loadEntryForDelivery`, `loadMergedSinglePage`: what routes and SSR render.
- [server/content-types.ts](server/content-types.ts) — content type config, directories, URL patterns.
- Validate against Zod schemas from [shared/schema.ts](shared/schema.ts).

Do **not** add entry-level `context:` (`when_to_use` / `target_audience` / `goals`) on `_common.yml` or locale YAML — that brief was retired with adapt-with-AI. Prefer content-type `strategy` / field `fill_intent` and component-registry `when_to_use` for authoring guidance. Brand voice remains in `site_<name>/brand-context.yml` (read via `/api/brand-context`).

## Key Files Reference

### Configuration
- [vite.config.ts](vite.config.ts) — Path aliases: `@/*` → `client/src`, `@shared/*` → `shared`
- [sites.yml](sites.yml) — sites, domains, content folders, inheritance, content repos
- [tailwind.config.cjs](tailwind.config.cjs) — app-wide type scale, radius, spacing tokens

### Per-site content
- `site_<name>/brand-context.yml` — brand voice/tone
- `site_<name>/theme.json` — site colors and palettes (backgrounds, text, accents, courses, `colors.light` / `colors.dark`); overrides `client/src/index.css` defaults. A site without one uses its `inherit_components_from` parent's.
- `site_<name>/image-registry.json` — media gallery registry

### Schema & Validation
- [shared/schema.ts](shared/schema.ts) — Zod schemas (pages, sections) and Drizzle tables
- [scripts/validation/service.ts](scripts/validation/service.ts) — content validation service

### Component Registry
- [server/component-registry.ts](server/component-registry.ts) — loads component metadata, versions, examples, schemas
- [shared/component-registry/](shared/component-registry/) — shared types, used by every site (app repo)
- `site_<name>/component-registry/` — site types (content repo); children inherit via `inherit_components_from`
- The same type in both trees fails at boot.

### Utilities
- [shared/locale.ts](shared/locale.ts) — `normalizeLocale()` handles en/es with fallbacks
- [shared/slugMappings.ts](shared/slugMappings.ts) — maps translated slugs to folder names
- [server/github.ts](server/github.ts) / [server/sync-state.ts](server/sync-state.ts) — content repo commits and pending-change tracking

## GitHub Sync

1. Edits mark files as modified in sync state.
2. Cloud Sync (or `commitAndPush` / `commitSingleFile`) commits to the site's content repo with `[Author: X] Message`.
3. GET `/api/github/sync-status` shows pending local/remote changes; conflicts can be pulled or force-pushed.

Needs `GITHUB_TOKEN` with write access to the content repos.

## Common Patterns & Conventions

### YAML Content Structure
- Top-level `meta`: SEO (title, description, robots, priority, change_frequency, redirects)
- `sections` array: each section has `type`, `variant`, `version`, its props inline, and wrapper settings (`background`, `paddingY`, `marginY`)

### API Response Format
Success: `{ ...contentData }` or `{ success: true, data: ... }`
Error: `{ error: "message" }` with appropriate HTTP status

### Error Handling
- **Content not found**: 404 with `{ error: "Content not found" }`
- **Validation fails**: 400 with `{ error: "...", details: [...] }`
- **Auth required**: 401; in dev mode auth can be bypassed with `X-Debug-Token`

### Component Development
Follow the skill [.agents/skills/internal-new-component/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/internal-new-component/SKILL.md) (reuse check, written spec, build, verify). Variant files in `client/src/components/{type}/variants/` are auto-registered by [client/src/components/sectionRegistry.ts](client/src/components/sectionRegistry.ts).

## Debugging Tips

- **Cache issues**: POST `/api/debug/clear-sitemap-cache`, `/api/debug/clear-schema-cache`
- **Token validation**: POST `/api/debug/validate-token` checks Breathecode API integration
- **Session check**: POST `/api/debug/check-session` verifies token expiration
- **Schema mismatch**: run `scripts/validation/service.ts` or POST `/api/validation/run`

## Important Notes

1. **Content is YAML, not database**: page content lives in `site_*` YAML. The app SQLite databases (`data/app.db`, `data/<site>/app.db`) hold users, sessions, conversations, error logs, pipeline and migration state — not page content.
2. **Locale fallback**: missing locale defaults to "en" via `normalizeLocale()`.
3. **GitHub token required for content commits**: without `GITHUB_TOKEN`, Cloud Sync cannot push.
4. **Theme**: site colors come from `site_<name>/theme.json` (or the parent's); `client/src/index.css` is the shared fallback layer.
